From: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ufs-qcom: use firmware-managed vops and fix initialization on ACPI platforms

When booting via ACPI (device QCOM24A5, e.g. under UEFI firmware), the UFS
host controller, PHY, and clocks are pre-initialized by system firmware.
Using the default DeviceTree variant ops (ufs_hba_qcom_vops) breaks boot
because the driver attempts bare-metal clock scaling, interconnect lookups,
and reset asserting on cold boot which desynchronizes the link.

Fix this cleanly by:
1. Routing ACPI platforms to ufs_hba_qcom_sa8255p_vops (firmware-managed design)
   both in ufs_qcom_probe() and in ufs_qcom_acpi_match[].
2. For safety, also ensure ufs_qcom_init(), ufs_qcom_icc_init(), and
   ufs_qcom_power_up_sequence() safely return without NULL dereferences
   under ACPI.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -493,6 +493,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_power_up_sequence(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	enum phy_mode mode;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (has_acpi_companion(hba->dev))
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * HW ver 5 can only support up to HS-G5 Rate-A due to HW limitations.
 	 * If the HS-G5 PHY gear is used, update host_params->hs_rate to Rate-A,
@@ -1514,6 +1517,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_icc_init(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 	struct device *dev = host->hba->dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (has_acpi_companion(dev))
+		return 0;
+
 	host->icc_ddr = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "ufs-ddr");
 	if (IS_ERR(host->icc_ddr))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(host->icc_ddr),
@@ -1572,6 +1578,7 @@ static int ufs_qcom_init(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	}
 
 	/* Fire up the reset controller. Failure here is non-fatal. */
+	host->rcdev.dev = dev;
 	host->rcdev.of_node = dev->of_node;
 	host->rcdev.ops = &ufs_qcom_reset_ops;
 	host->rcdev.owner = dev->driver->owner;
@@ -2972,7 +2979,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	const struct ufs_hba_variant_ops *vops;
 	const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata *drvdata = device_get_match_data(dev);
 
-	if (drvdata && drvdata->vops)
+	if (has_acpi_companion(dev))
+		vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_sa8255p_vops;
+	else if (drvdata && drvdata->vops)
 		vops = drvdata->vops;
 	else
 		vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_vops;
@@ -3020,7 +3029,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, ufs_qcom_of_match);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ACPI
 static const struct acpi_device_id ufs_qcom_acpi_match[] = {
-	{ "QCOM24A5" },
+	{ "QCOM24A5", (kernel_ulong_t)&ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
 	{ },
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, ufs_qcom_acpi_match);
